From a4595634a70d76caa63b360f8ea57ed90c38a662 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samson1357924 <98934496+samson1357924@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 05:19:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] acp: consider phantom jacks without kcontrol as present

Some sound cards (in particular ASoC devices like Chromebooks with the
sof-rt5682 machine driver) do not expose a kcontrol for phantom jacks
such as "Speaker Phantom". The kernel creates phantom jacks only for
HDA devices; ASoC has no phantom jack support.

Without this, paths that have phantom jacks in their required-any list
(e.g. analog-output-speaker) are discarded during probing, leaving no
available output ports. All analog profiles then become unavailable and
the card ends up without any sink (Dummy Output only).

Treat phantom jacks without a kcontrol as present, keeping the path and
its port. The port availability stays unknown, which matches the
state.plugged/unplugged settings in the path configuration files.

Upstream-MR: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/pipewire/pipewire/-/merge_requests/5428
Signed-off-by: samson1357924 <98934496+samson1357924@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 spa/plugins/alsa/acp/alsa-mixer.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/alsa-mixer.c b/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/alsa-mixer.c
index 84c5cc2..320a6b1 100644
--- a/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/alsa-mixer.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/alsa/acp/alsa-mixer.c
@@ -2011,6 +2011,15 @@ static int jack_probe(pa_alsa_jack *j, pa_alsa_mapping *mapping, snd_mixer_t *m)
     } else {
         if (j->required != PA_ALSA_REQUIRED_IGNORE)
             return -1;
+
+        /* A phantom jack (e.g. "Speaker Phantom") describes an always
+         * present device such as internal speakers. Some sound cards
+         * (in particular ASoC devices) do not expose a corresponding
+         * ALSA kcontrol, so treat the jack as present in that case
+         * and keep the associated path. */
+        if (j->required_any != PA_ALSA_REQUIRED_IGNORE &&
+            strstr(j->name, "Phantom") != NULL)
+            j->path->req_any_present = true;
     }
 
     return 0;
